course: dictionary
lesson: 13833
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them all, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word: they are its context, and they give you clues. «Mia won the game of jacks by catching the ball every time.» The words game and ball point to the playground game, so jacks means the game.
explain: «Dad used a jack to lift the car so he could change the tyre.» Here a jack is a tool. The words lift, car and tyre are your clues. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Jacks is the plural of jack, so it can mean more than one thing. A word that looks the same can have a different meaning in a different sentence. Do not stop at the first meaning you know. Read on and check the clues.
fact: Jacks is the plural of jack.
fact: Jacks is a children's game where you toss a small ball and pick up small metal or plastic pieces called jacks before catching the ball.
fact: A jack is also a playing card with a picture of a young man, worth between 10 and the queen.
fact: A jack is a tool that lifts a car off the ground, for example to change a tyre.
fact: Informal, in Australia: «jacks» can mean police, and «be jack of» means be tired of.
exercise: «Mia won the game of jacks by catching the ball every time.» What are jacks in this sentence? | Small animals that hop | A tool for lifting a car | Playing cards with pictures | *A children's game with small pieces to pick up
exercise: «Dad used a jack to lift the car so he could change the tyre.» What is a jack here? | A children's game | A card with a picture of a young man | A kind of police officer | *A tool that lifts a car off the ground
exercise: «In the card game, Sam was thrilled to pick up the jack of hearts.» What is a jack? | *A playing card with a picture of a young man | A small ball that bounces | A tool for changing tyres | A piece of metal for a game
test: «Our class is playing jacks at break time, tossing the ball and picking up the pieces.» What does jacks mean here? | *The children's game | Two friends | A playing card | A car tool
test: «Beth is jack of waiting for the bus, so she walks instead.» What does «be jack of» mean? | Be happy with | Be afraid of | Be late for | *Be tired of
exam: «Tom lifted the car with a jack, then tossed the ball in a game of jacks.» What does jack mean in the first part? | A small metal piece in a game | *A tool that lifts a car off the ground | A kind of ball | A playing card with a picture of a young man
